{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1410108-adding-choices-to-sail","id":1410108,"title":"Adding choices to Sail","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-24T12:05:33-07:00","id":1410108,"title":"Adding choices to Sail","content":"After a very muddled first encounter with naval combat, my players and I had a conversation about the rules and where they fell apart. By our analysis, the rules as written occupy an odd space between extended checks and true combat rules--there's marginally more complexity than simply rolling the same check over and over again, and you have certain choices to make during a combat... but not enough. It still <i>basically </i>boils down to rolling rolling Positioning until you have enough momentum to ram. At the same time, we don't want things to get as crunchy as, say, the combat system, not when the majority of the party is likely sidelined. We also didn't want to have to rewrite Charms if we could possibly avoid it.<br /> <br /> The core of the idea is to add choice to Positioning. Rather than a single generic roll, I broke it down into several options, each with their own benefits and drawbacks. A few more stratagem options, a pair of tags, and... hopefully this is a little more fun? (I'm not touching number bloat; that's kind of a separate issue)<br /> <br /> --------------<br /> <br /> The following stratagems involve two new tags: Advantage and Disadvantage. The benefits of a stratagem with the Advantage tag last for as long as your momentum is higher than your opponent\u2019s, while the penalties inflicted by stratgems with the Disadvantage tag last until the vessel uses the Recover stratagem.<br /> <br /> When using the Positioning stratagem, you may select one of the following additional benefits:<ul><li><b>Catch the Wind (Advantage):</b> You tack into the wind or current, allowing you to add your ship\u2019s Speed to naval maneuver checks instead of Maneuverability.</li> <li><b>Close (Advantage):</b> You tack closer to your foe, granting you double 9s on attempts to ram or board your foe\u2014but when you attempt a broadside or escape stratagem, your opponent gains double 9s on their opposing roll. Using the Open Range stratagem ends this benefit.</li> <li><b>Double Time (Disadvantage):</b> You exhort your crew to greater efforts, removing any Advantage your foe is currently benefiting from. In the aftermath, your crew is fatigued, inflicting a cumulative -1 penalty to Sail checks for the remainder of the scene.</li> <li><b>Open Range (Advantage):</b> You attempt to open distance with your foe, granting double 9s on attempts to use the broadside and escape stratagems against your foe\u2014but when you attempt a ram or boarding action stratagem, your opponent gains double 9s on their opposing roll. Using the Close stratagem ends this benefit.</li> <li><b>Recover:</b> Your crew scrambles to conduct emergency repairs. Remove any ongoing Disadvantage conditions your vessel is suffering from, and reduce the wound penalty due to Hull damage by 1 for the remainder of the scene. However, your distraction grants your opponent double 9s on their opposing roll.</li> </ul><br /> The following new Stratagems or expanded Stratagems are available to everyone.<ul><li><b>Boarding Action</b>: One new option is added.<ul><li><b>Heroic Assault (5 momentum):</b> The Exalt-- and other Exalts, with stunts-- hops onto the other ship somehow without linking ships together</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Broadside:</b> The Broadside stratagem gets broken down into several options.<ul><li><b>Cut the Sails (2 momentum, Disadvantage):</b> You target your foe\u2019s sails, oars, or other means of propulsion. They suffer a -1 penalty to their Maneuverability and Speed. This penalty increases by one for every three threshold successes.</li> <li><b>Rake the Decks (6 momentum):</b> You order your gunners to target the enemy\u2019s crew directly. A crew has a Magnitude track just like a battle group; a successful Rake the Decks stratagem inflicts one point of Magnitude damage per threshold success.</li> <li><b>Ship Killer (5 momentum):</b> You gunners attempt to destroy your foe\u2019s hull, inflicting one point of Hull damage, plus one additional point for every four threshold successes. Particularly powerful weapons, such as artifact ballista or implosion bows, can grant bonus damage.</li> <li><b>Target Rudder (3 momentum, Disadvantage):</b> You attempt to damage your foe\u2019s steering, inflicting a -2 penalty to their Maneuverability.</li> <li><b>Target Weapons (6 momentum):</b> You order your gunners to aim squarely at a foe\u2019s weapons, damaging them preventing them from using the Broadside stratagem. Weapons destroyed this way cannot be repaired without prolonged effort.</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Cross the T (3 momentum, Advantage):</b> You chart a course perpendicular to your foe, allowing your full battery of weapons to strike while the majority of the enemy\u2019s have difficulty targeting you. You gain double 9s on Broadside checks, and your opponent cannot attempt Broadside stratagems against you.</li> <li><b>Lure (4 momentum, Advantage):</b> You pressure a foe, driving them on a course of your choosing. This allows you to force a foe into a reef, disadvantageous current, or other environmental hazard.</li> <li><b>Ram</b>: The Ram stratagem gets broken down into several options.<ul><li><b>Hull Breaker</b> <b>(7 momentum):</b> Ram your foe, as the normal Ram stratagem</li> <li><b>Ram Breaker (8 momentum):</b> You send your ship crashing into your enemy\u2019s ram at a perpendicular angle, breaking it off.</li> <li><b>Shatter Oars (2 momentum, Disadvantage):</b> You rip along the side of your foe\u2019s vessel, breaking off oars and other means of propulsion close to water level and inflicting a -1 penalty to their Maneuverability and Speed. This penalty increases by one for every three threshold successes.</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Spot Reef (2 momentum):</b> Use your Perception in place of Wits when attempting this stratagem. On a success, you notice a previously-unseen hazard in the immediate area.</li> </ul><br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12314,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","user":"Grod_the_giant","date":". 09-05-2020, 08:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T01:29:33-07:00","id":1410245,"title":"","content":"Having run a naval campaign for 2 years with a Sail Supernal, I can unfortunately tell you: none of this will matter because there's nothing that can challenge a Sailing Solar on the Seas, even Sans Supernal. No maneuver or trick changes the fact that Solar excellencies are too powerful for gaining momentum and Sail is all about momentum. <br /> <br /> I like what you wrote, but its like giving a swiss army knife to a Melee Dawn fighting a half blind dog.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T07:40:05-07:00","id":1410287,"title":"","content":"My sailor had 5 dots and Salty Dog Method, and he was struggling with enemies who had a 12-die pool (Maneuverability +2, Crew +2, Sail 5, Wits 3); I wound up reducing the enemy die pools so he could build up enough momentum to sink ram someone before the agata-mounted Dawn and Zenith finished hopping from ship to ship killing everyone manually. Is it just the Immortal Mariner's Advantage tree that's the problem?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12314,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","user":"Grod_the_giant","date":". 08-25-2020, 10:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T08:13:19-07:00","id":1410296,"title":"","content":"Sounds like Sorcerous Overlord is more referring to how naval combat being opposed rolls instead of back-and-forth roll vs. static value means you get twice as much bang for your mote and therefore can afford bigger excellencies to stay ahead of those twelve opposing dice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T12:24:24-07:00","id":1410362,"title":"","content":"From previous threads, I'm very sure that's what Sorcerous Overlord is talking about.<br /> <br /> A 12 dice pool for your NPCs was probably hiding things a bit (8 base dice is already extremely good unless we're talking other Exalted captains, with a crew that's also one of the best on the ocean having to average Sail 4+ among them, in a dedicated war vessel to get that +2 Maneuverability rating).<br /> <br /> But if your PC already has Sail 5, we can guess Wits is 3+ in there unless they didn't read the sailing rules at all before making this character, plus a specialty, plus +5 dice every round? That's already a statistical win for the PC with a +0 Maneuverability ship and a +0 crew. Tossing on Salty Dog Method and Immortal Mariner's Advantage is just rubbing salt in the wound.<br /> <br /> The issue of the other PCs going faster is that the book isn't entirely clear how to handle that situation. The way the rules are written, normal combat doesn't come in until a Boarding Action happens.... though the rules don't really account for Exalted that can leap from ship to ship, or fly around. Even with a Solar Sail Supernal easily trouncing mortal ships with minimal investment, it's going to look like a snails pace if you let other PCs finish normal combat with an enemy crew between Positioning rolls and completely bypass the sailing rules.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T12:54:57-07:00","id":1410371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1410108-adding-choices-to-sail?p=1410245#post1410245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having run a naval campaign for 2 years with a Sail Supernal, I can unfortunately tell you: none of this will matter because there's nothing that can challenge a Sailing Solar on the Seas, even Sans Supernal. No maneuver or trick changes the fact that Solar excellencies are too powerful for gaining momentum and Sail is all about momentum.<br /> <br /> I like what you wrote, but its like giving a swiss army knife to a Melee Dawn fighting a half blind dog.</div> </div> </div> </div>This.<br /> <br /> But to avoid just echoing others, I did try to expand navel combat. The space combat rules I made for my Heaven's Reach came provided plenty of other things for other PC's to do on a vessel. When testing it myself it was a bit complex, but it worked pretty well. For as well as Sail possibly allows it to work.<br /> <br /> One day I'll finish that ship homebrew.<br /> <br /> Also, with the ship we got in Arms, I do not recommend swapping Speed for manueverability in tests ever. The rest of them? Sail is so broken that making material for it is akin to making the foundation of a city in a swamp. Your ideas are good, but no matter how good they are they're still on top of a very bad base system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":1183,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","user":"Sandact6","date":". 08-25-2020, 03:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T12:58:08-07:00","id":1410372,"title":"","content":"Don't get me wrong, I'm not looking to contend with a Sail supernal--my player had a few dots from his background and picked up the rest once it became clear the next arc of the story was going to revolve around the Lintha, and maybe the Peleps. There will be God-Blooded, Dragonblooded, demons, sorcerers, sea monsters, and even a few Infernals running around before things are through. There will be enough magic bull**** around to provide the occasional challenge, and I'm happy to have him wreck any amount of mortal opposition... as long as we're having fun and not gritting our teeth at the rules. <br /> <br /> If it helps, pretend these changes are for a Dragonblooded or heroic mortals campaign?<br /> <br /> Edit: Sandact6, would you mind sharing a link?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T14:00:53-07:00","id":1410389,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.mediafire.com/file/b572tcf24j4kxjv/Heaven%27s%20Reach%20Guidebook.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Here in Chapter 6</a> for the ship combat homebrew, and <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1QasCNUqOLzdGh8xtS6N9KZ9ypjsflllrbq7WzwJgDZU/edit\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> for some artifact ship samples.<br /> <br /> Note it's very tailored for spaceship combat. Some things could be ported over without difficulty I'd imagine tho.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}